e from h2-g1 area. After Kg5, White king only has g1 and h1 squares (if not in check). Then I can push c5-c4 with king support later. However, White king might get stalemated if I'm not careful.  \n\nGiven winning position, simplest is to push passed pawn. **P: c5-c4** is direct and forces White to react. White king can go to g1 or h1 (only legal squares). That’s fine.  \n\nReason: c5-c4 advances my most advanced passed pawn toward promotion, with tempo. The White king is far away and cannot capture. Next move I can support with bishop or king. This forces the game toward a quick queen.  \n\nAnswer: P: c5-c4"}
