 square (f4) that directly threatens the white king at g3. This puts immediate pressure and could force the white king to move, disrupting any potential plans. Additionally, it opens lines for the bishop at e3 to possibly support or create threats. It’s an aggressive move that capitalizes on our material advantage and keeps the initiative.\n\nAnswer: K: g5-f4"}
