ter/kingside. B: c2-b3 also frees it. But b3 is attacked by pawn? No, white has no pawns. So both safe.\n\nI think fastest is to free the c3 pawn. So move bishop from c2.\n\nI choose B: c2-d3 or B: c2-b3. Which is better? d3 is closer to white king, possibly more active. b3 is on long diagonal a2-g8? Actually b3 to f7 diagonal, but not directly towards white king. d3 is central and eyes f1/g2 area. I'll pick B: c2-d3.\n\nBut also consider that after B: c2-d3, white king might move to f2 or something, but it cannot capture bishop because not attacked. It's safe.\n\nThus, B: c2-d3 seems best.\n\nReason: To quickly free the advanced pawn on c3, allowing it to promote to a queen within two moves, after which checkmate is trivial. This is faster than advancing other pawns and utilizes the most advanced pawn.\n\nAnswer: B: c2-d3"}
